# SITE-V1 permanent governance

- Use the current task, `AGENTS.md`, applicable local rules, accepted ADRs,
  current contracts and schemas, durable documentation, code and tests as
  operational authority.
- Keep every commit safe for public history and preserve the private/public data
  boundary.
- Never infer factual review or invent authorization the current task did not
  grant.
- Local transfer of the named projection needs explicit task authority; if
  already granted, do not re-ask. It is not commit, visibility, deployment or
  publication. Locally mutating this repository is not publication, even if the
  remote is public.
- Do not stage, commit, push, change remotes/visibility, deploy or publish unless
  the current task explicitly authorizes that exact action.
- Keep increments small, inspect all changes and close with the increment
  report required by `AGENTS.md`.
